Kind: widen
Issue: #904
Holds open: the window between a writer taking the slot at prod_tail and publishing it -- 1 ms of thread_switch(SWITCH_OPTION_WAIT) after the copy and before flipc2_produce_commit(), so that a second writer of the pipe arrives while the first still holds the slot, on one processor as on four; with the fix the second waits on the writers' lock.  Without it, 904-no-writers-lock was caught 3 of 4 at d9e0402c on OMEGA: in one KVM boot at -smp 4 the two writers of musl_test's [33] never overlapped.  Only musl_test uses a pipe in a boot, so nothing else meets the delay
Run: --entry 14 600 -smp 4

diff --git a/uros/src/lib/libposix-uros/posix_pipe.c b/uros/src/lib/libposix-uros/posix_pipe.c
index ccc83588..f21df38b 100644
--- a/uros/src/lib/libposix-uros/posix_pipe.c
+++ b/uros/src/lib/libposix-uros/posix_pipe.c
@@ -40,6 +40,8 @@
 #include <mach_init.h>          /* mach_task_self */
 #include <mach/vm_inherit.h>
 #include "mach.h"               /* MIG: vm_inherit */
+#include <mach/thread_switch.h>	/* 904-widen-write-window */
+#include <mach/mach_syscalls.h>	/* 904-widen-write-window */
 
 /*
  * flipc2.h's flipc2_ring_count() never reads its `hdr', and this library is
@@ -381,6 +383,8 @@ __uros_pipe_write(struct uros_pipe *p, const struct uros_pipe_iov *iov,
 		d->param[1] = 0;
 		d->param[2] = 0;
 		d->status = 0;
+		/* 904-widen-write-window: the slot held 1 ms before it is published */
+		(void)syscall_thread_switch(MACH_PORT_NULL, SWITCH_OPTION_WAIT, 1);
 		flipc2_produce_commit(ch);
 		done += chunk;
 	}
